## 11. Database Security

The database should be protected using:

* User authentication
* Password protection
* Access control
* Regular backups
* Data validation
* Secure database connections

Only authorized users should be allowed to access or modify important information.

## 12. Data Backup

Regular backups should be performed to prevent data loss.

Backup methods can include:

* Daily backups
* Weekly full backups
* Cloud backup
* Recovery procedures

## 13. Data Management

The system should maintain accurate and organized data.

Important practices include:

* Avoid duplicate records
* Validate user input
* Keep ticket history
* Update outdated knowledge-base articles
* Remove unnecessary data when appropriate

## 14. Scalability

The database should be designed so that it can support an increasing number of:

* Students
* Tickets
* Support staff
* Knowledge articles
* Feedback records

A scalable database allows the system to grow without major changes.

## 15. Benefits

A properly designed database provides:

* Organized information
* Faster data retrieval
* Better ticket tracking
* Reliable record keeping
* Improved security
* Easier reporting
* Better system performance

## 16. Conclusion

The database design provides the foundation for the Virtual Customer Support System. It connects students, tickets, support staff, knowledge-base articles, and feedback in an organized manner. Proper security, backup, and scalability can make the system reliable for academic use.
